    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1740">

                <pb facs="1266" n="1150" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg1150"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 718.1915/238.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Endicott to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">San José</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-06-24">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 24, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Costa Rican Minister for Foreign Affairs has verbally requested me to inform you
                    that an extraordinary mission from Panama headed by Santiago de la Guardia
                    accredited as Envoy Extraordinary and Minister Plenipotentiary has arrived at
                    San José with the object of reaching an agreement to modify the boundary
                    question decided by the Chief Justice; that the Costa Rican Government refuses
                    to treat of this matter with Guardia as it considers that it should be settled
                    by the judgment; and that the only thing that the Costa Rican Government desires
                    is to proceed as soon as possible to matter of delimitation, for which it counts
                    on the good offices of the United States.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Endicott.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
